# Intent
  arrangeManager: discovery, slot auto-allocation, placement, reswing.

# Helpers
  @fn mkAm(harness, opts)  @ 7-12
  @fn seedTracks(h, specs)  @ 18-40
      -- Seed two arbitrary tracks and a per-track item list. Returns the
      -- track tokens so each test can name them. The harness's default
      -- bindTake(take1) is unrelated — we manage these via setProjectTracks
      -- so am sees them in CountTracks/GetTrack order.

# Cases
  @case 'projectTracks lists every track in REAPER order with item count'  [harness]  @ 47-63
  @case 'trackSlots auto-allocates slot indices for live takes'  [harness]  @ 70-84
  @case 'tracksTakes assigns slotIdx to every grouped take'  [harness]  @ 88-106
  @case 'ensureSlots is idempotent — second read does not reallocate'  [harness]  @ 110-121
  @case 'hasPlacedTakes ignores parked takes, sees placed instances'  [harness]  @ 125-134
  @case 'ownerTrack resolves a parked take to its logical track, not scratch'  [harness]  @ 141-155
  @case 'renameSlot writes SetTakeName across every matching item'  [harness]  @ 162-178
  @case 'deleteSlot removes every matching item and prunes the dict entry'  [harness]  @ 182-200
  @case 'createAndDropMidi mints slot 0, creates a take, names it'  [harness]  @ 207-223
  @case 'createAndDropMidi allocates lowest-free index across calls'  [harness]  @ 227-238
  @case 'dropInstance pools to an existing slot'  [harness]  @ 242-253
  @case 'dropInstance overwrites a take already starting at the drop position'  [harness]  @ 257-274
  @case 'createAndDropMidi overwrites a take already starting at the create position'  [harness]  @ 278-293
  @case 'dropInstance returns nil for missing slot or missing track'  [harness]  @ 297-303
  @case 'duplicateTake clones a MIDI take into a pooled sibling'  [harness]  @ 307-322
  @case 'dropInstance and duplicateTake name the new take after the slot'  [harness]  @ 326-337
  @case 'duplicateTake returns nil for a missing track'  [harness]  @ 341-349
  @case 'dropInstance carries the sibling MIDI events into the new instance'  [harness]  @ 353-363
  @case 'duplicateTake carries the source MIDI events into the clone'  [harness]  @ 367-378
  @case 'startIsClear only collides on an exact start match (item ~= exceptItem)'  [harness]  @ 382-397
  @case 'createAndDropMidi returns nil when no track exists'  [harness]  @ 401-406
  @case 'keyForSlot maps 0..61 through util.toBase62'  [harness]  @ 413-422
  @case 'takesUsing scans each take swing map (ds) for the named swing'  [harness]  @ 429-447
  @case 'tempersInUse unions take/project temper names, minus the 12EDO floor'  [harness]  @ 450-464
  @case 'tracksTakes relayouts on read: an OPEN take grows to its source length'  [harness]  @ 474-483
  @case 'build relayout: OPEN takes fill to source; an earlier one capped at its gap (no overlap)'  [harness]  @ 486-497
  @case 'build relayout: an OPEN take whose item outruns its shrunk source is pulled back'  [harness]  @ 500-508
  @case 'a later take truncates an earlier one; deleting the later regrows it'  [harness]  @ 512-526
  @case 'resizeTake stores a numeric natural; ≥ source demotes back to util.OPEN'  [harness]  @ 530-546
  @case 'audio take longer than its source keeps its length across a move'  [harness]  @ 549-564
  @case 'trimmed audio take keeps its trim across a move (no balloon to source)'  [harness]  @ 567-579
  @case 'moveTake shifts start; refused on start-collision; returns ok flag'  [harness]  @ 583-594
  @case 'resizeTake writes natural; rendered is min(natural, source, gap)'  [harness]  @ 598-609
  @case 'deleteTake removes the item, leaving the other take intact'  [harness]  @ 613-624
  @case 'deleteTake parks a slot\'s last instance; the slot survives, greyed'  [harness]  @ 630-646
  @case 'deleteTake of a non-last instance deletes outright (no park)'  [harness]  @ 650-665
  @case 're-dropping from a parked slot re-materialises off the keeper'  [harness]  @ 669-682
  @case 'deleteSlot forever-deletes: live instances and the parked keeper'  [harness]  @ 686-699
  @case 'deleteSlot forever-deletes the pool per-event metadata'  [harness]  @ 703-714
  @case 'mintParkedTake shows the new slot at once; isParkedTake flags scratch-hosted takes'  [harness]  @ 718-733
  @case 'vary replaces the instance with one of a fresh variant slot'  [harness]  @ 740-762
  @case 'vary numbers from the family high-water mark; a variant of a variant joins the family'  [harness]  @ 766-777
  @case 'vary refuses on a slot with a single instance'  [harness]  @ 781-789
  @case 'findTake resolves a REAPER take handle back to its grid take-shape'  [harness]  @ 796-810
  @case 'initialCursor reads the selected item: its take track and start'  [harness]  @ 814-826
  @case 'initialCursor falls back to the edit cursor and selected track'  [harness]  @ 830-839
  @case 'initialCursor defaults to track 0 when nothing is selected'  [harness]  @ 843-851
  @case 'editCursorQN reads the REAPER edit cursor'  [harness]  @ 858-863
  @case 'setEditCursorQN moves the REAPER edit cursor'  [harness]  @ 867-872
  @case 'loopRangeQN returns the project loop range'  [harness]  @ 876-883
  @case 'loopRangeQN is nil when no loop is set'  [harness]  @ 887-891
  @case 'setLoopRangeQN writes the project loop range'  [harness]  @ 895-902
  @case 'loopTo brackets a span: loop range, repeat on, cursor at its start'  [harness]  @ 906-914
  @case 'loopTo leaves the cursor alone when the play head is inside the span'  [harness]  @ 918-927
  @case 'clearLoopRange removes the project loop range'  [harness]  @ 931-937
  @case 'playPositionQN is nil when the transport is stopped'  [harness]  @ 941-945
  @case 'playPositionQN returns the play head qn while playing'  [harness]  @ 949-954
  @case 'seekInstance takes the instance whose rendered span holds qn'  [harness]  @ 961-975
  @case 'seekInstance spans are half-open — the end belongs to the next'  [harness]  @ 979-988
  @case 'seekInstance from a gap travels forwards by default, backwards when asked'  [harness]  @ 992-1004
  @case 'seekInstance falls back to the other direction when its own is empty'  [harness]  @ 1008-1018
  @case 'seekInstance ignores instances of other slots'  [harness]  @ 1022-1034
  @case 'seekInstance matches on the rendered span, not the source span'  [harness]  @ 1038-1050
  @case 'seekInstance is nil for a slot whose only take is parked'  [harness]  @ 1054-1064
  @case 'projectEndQN is 0 for a project with no items'  [harness]  @ 1068-1072
  @case 'projectEndQN reports the largest take end across all tracks'  [harness]  @ 1076-1085
  @case 'freeSpan is the gap to the next take, and unbounded past the last'  [harness]  @ 1092-1102
  @case 'duplicateBelow places a pooled clone at the append point'  [harness]  @ 1106-1122
  @case 'duplicateBelow refuses where a truncating neighbour leaves no room'  [harness]  @ 1126-1142
  @case 'duplicateBelow refuses where the gap is shorter than the natural length'  [harness]  @ 1146-1157
  @case 'duplicateBelow refuses on exact-start collision at the destination'  [harness]  @ 1161-1171
  @case 'duplicateBelow refuses on audio takes'  [harness]  @ 1175-1184
  @case 'duplicateUnpooledBelow mints a fresh slot and copies the MIDI blob'  [harness]  @ 1188-1208
  @case 'duplicateUnpooledBelow forks the source per-event metadata onto the fresh pool'  [harness]  @ 1214-1225
  @case 'duplicateUnpooledBelow parks the clone for want of room'  [harness]  @ 1229-1246
  @case 'duplicateUnpooledBelow refuses on audio'  [harness]  @ 1250-1258
  @case 'newTakeBelow creates an empty MIDI take of the asked-for length at the append point'  [harness]  @ 1262-1283
  @case 'newTakeBelow parks the take for want of room'  [harness]  @ 1287-1299
  @case 'newTakeBelow measures the room against the length asked for'  [harness]  @ 1303-1314
  @case 'newTakeBelow refuses on audio'  [harness]  @ 1318-1326
  @case 'distinct pool guids on different tracks get distinct colourIdx'  [harness]  @ 1331-1344
  @case 'pooled instances on different tracks share one colourIdx'  [harness]  @ 1348-1358
  @case 'createAndDropMidi stamps I_CUSTOMCOLOR on the new take'  [harness]  @ 1362-1370
  @case 'duplicateUnpooledBelow strips the source colour and mints a fresh one'  [harness]  @ 1374-1390
  @case 'placement does not overwrite a pre-existing take colour (preserve override)'  [harness]  @ 1394-1406
  @case 'a recycled take handle reports the new item\'s pool, not the dead take\'s'  [harness]  @ 1411-1434

